thunderbolt: stream: do not enable E2E flow control on the Tx ring.
On incite's Falcon Ridge controllers a Tx ring with E2E never gets credits; stopping it wedges the NHI
and every later config read times out (results/kernel/tb-loopback-20261006). Same failure as the
thunderbolt_net revert 1881f2efbf7f. Rx keeps E2E.

--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/stream.c
@@ -553,8 +553,13 @@
 	struct tb_ring *ring;
 	int ret, e2e_tx_hop;
 
+	/*
+	 * No E2E flow control on the Tx ring: some host routers never return
+	 * the credits and the ring wedges (see the thunderbolt_net revert
+	 * 1881f2efbf7f). Rx keeps E2E.
+	 */
 	ring = tb_ring_alloc_tx(xd->tb->nhi, -1, sdev->ring_size,
-				RING_FLAG_FRAME | RING_FLAG_E2E);
+				RING_FLAG_FRAME);
 	if (!ring)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	sdev->tx_ring.ring = ring;
